From: HP-UX 11.23 ia64 port notes
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] ia64-hpux: default off two RTL passes that crash on this target

cc1 segfaults in the RTL PRE pass (gcse.c, ILP32 -O2) and the RTL
loop-invariant-motion pass (loop-invariant.c, LP64 -O1+) on pointer-heavy and
template-heavy input. ia64-linux of the same vintage does not: target-specific
RTL feeding shared passes. Default both off so the shipped compiler cannot hit
them; tree-level LIM still runs, so the optimisation cost is modest.
-fgcse / -fmove-loop-invariants re-enable them explicitly.
--- a/gcc/config/ia64/ia64.c
+++ b/gcc/config/ia64/ia64.c
@@ -6093,6 +6103,22 @@
   if (TARGET_AUTO_PIC)
     target_flags |= MASK_CONST_GP;
 
+  /* HP-UX-local workaround (2026-07-23): on ia64-hpux this compiler segfaults in
+     the RTL PRE pass (gcse.c, ILP32 at -O2) and the RTL loop-invariant-motion pass
+     (loop-invariant.c, LP64 at -O1+) on template-heavy/pointer-heavy code; the
+     ia64-linux configurations of the same era do not exhibit this (target-specific
+     RTL feeding shared passes).  Default both passes OFF so the shipped compiler
+     cannot hit the crashes; tree-level LIM still runs, so the optimization cost is
+     modest.  Users may re-enable explicitly (-fgcse / -fmove-loop-invariants) at
+     their own risk.  See toolchain notes; candidate for a real fix later.  */
+  if (TARGET_HPUX)
+    {
+      if (!global_options_set.x_flag_gcse)
+	flag_gcse = 0;
+      if (!global_options_set.x_flag_move_loop_invariants)
+	flag_move_loop_invariants = 0;
+    }
+
   /* Numerous experiment shows that IRA based loop pressure
      calculation works better for RTL loop invariant motion on targets
      with enough (>= 32) registers.  It is an expensive optimization.
